    torchtitan engine: working CP for kimi_k3 (module-internal Ulysses)
    
    The engine's CP path had never been exercised end to end; wiring it for
    kimi_k3 surfaced five defects, all fixed here:
    
    1. context_parallel_load_balancer: kimi_k3's module-internal CP requires
       contiguous rank-ordered seq shards; upstream's default 'headtail'
       balancer permutes the sequence and silently breaks causal order
       (kimi parallelize now raises on it). Kimi gets None; upstream-CP
       models keep the torchtitan default.
    2. _get_data_parallel_mesh returned the 'fsdp' mesh, which in torchtitan
       is dp_shard x CP -- under cp>1 the DistributedSampler then split the
       DATA across cp ranks (crash at dp_shard=1: rank 1 not in [0,0], and
       silently wrong batches otherwise). Use the 'batch' mesh
       (dp_replicate x dp_shard), cp ranks share the batch.
    3. prepare_context_parallel_input requires positions in extra_kwargs;
       the engine keeps them in extra_inputs -> latent KeyError. Bridged.
    4. attention_masks: kimi is causal-only and never consumes them, and
       upstream BlockMask CP sharding requires seq %% (cp*128) == 0 which
       SFT batches don't guarantee -- masks bypass the CP shard for
       module-internal-CP models.
    5. verl's loss path (nested no-padding log_prob handling) assumes full
       sequences: keep labels full-length and all-gather the seq-sharded
       logits after the model call (differentiable, reduce-scatter
       backward). TODO: sharded-loss variant to avoid gathering [B,T,V]
       at long context.
    
    Verified (kimi_linear_194m fixture, 2x5060Ti): SFT dp1+cp2 runs a full
    epoch, step-1 loss 12.143 vs 12.149 single-GPU baseline (bf16 band),
    trajectories track; dp2 baseline unaffected.
    
